--TEST--
A `require` whose written path has no file behind it is `E0311`, and `<` on two objects whose class does not implement `Comparable` is `E0411` — `rule:statements/require-is-the-only-inclusion-construct`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: tools:php-differences/what-parses-but-behaves-differently
// The two rows of the PHP-differences chapter's "What parses but behaves
// differently" tables that end in a compile error.
class Box {
    public int $v = 0;
}

require "no-such-file.nvs";

Box $p = new Box();
Box $q = new Box();
echo $p < $q ? "lt" : "ge", "\n";
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0311]: `%s` cannot be loaded
  --> %s:9:9
  |
9 | require "no-such-file.nvs";
  |         ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ no file found at this path

error[E0411]: `Box` does not implement `Comparable`; ordering two objects with `<`/`<=`/`>`/`>=`/`<=>` requires it
   --> %s:13:6
   |
13 | echo $p < $q ? "lt" : "ge", "\n";
   |      ^^^^^^^ compared here
   = help: implement `Comparable`'s `compareTo(self $other): int` on the class

error: aborting due to 2 errors
